;; spec:   stdlib §4.15 (row future: "@f is (join f)"), §2.11, syntax §3.11
;; expect: reject
;; error:  no implementation of Deref for (Task i64)
;; roots:  ../../lib
;; covers: future
;; The note of row future says @f is (join f), as Clojure's is. The checker's rule for @ knows a Cell,
;; an Atom and a Weak (types/infer/solve.rs, solve_deref) and says this for a Task; an impl of the
;; builtin protocol Deref for Task in a program is accepted and then ignored by @ (the same error). So
;; the page and the code disagree, and this case pins what the code does. When @ on a Task lands this
;; case becomes an accept case with result 42, and case 655 gets an @f check.
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.async))

(defun main () -> i64
  (let ((f (future 42)))
    @f))
